  The best way to get out of trouble in NetHack is not to get into it in
the first place.  aka "Don't Do That Then" (DDTT).

  - Early GoP give +6 damage per hit and +3 to-hit.
  - Boots of Speed or Jumping are also early game breakers.  
    - Play a Knight with intrinsic chess knight move jumping to try
        out #jumping.


  Jumpstart your success rate by playing a Rogue.

  "Well, after 4 years playing nethack, 6 ascensions, millions of SD 
I finally understood that throwing daggers and become expert in 
daggers can save your life." - Davyduck

  "I am working on another Rogue!  The secret REALLY IS throwing early and
often!  So cool... =)" - SMG


    - Throw daggers early and often.  (You start with plenty.)
      - #adjust the daggers to 'Q' for easy quivering: 'QQ'
      - Turn on Autoquiver.
      - Fire the daggers using the 'f' command.
      - Use autopickup_exceptions to pick up daggers automatically.
          - Add the following lines to your NetHack Options file:

AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION="<*dagger*"
OPTIONS=autopickup


    - #Enhance daggers to Expert asap.
      - That will get you throwing an average of 2.5 daggers per fling.
        - That's 2.5x damage per fling.
        - Out to range Str/2.
        - Do Sokoban for strength
          - Str:18 gives +2 damage bonus.
          - Str/2 range of 9 means nothing should ever get to melee 
              range.
        - Gauntlets of Power give +6 damage bonus.  That's multiplied
            to +15 by a Rogue throwing Expert daggers.

    - Rogues get a backstab bonus on scared monsters (when NOT 
        #twoweaponing.)
        - Bonus averages to [(XL/2) + 1] per hit.  
            - 2.5x when flinging Expert daggers.
        - At XL:8 that's 2.5 x 5 = 12.5 just from the backstab bonus.

    - Scare monsters via:
        - Elbereth
            - A Rogue with Magicbane is in great shape.
            - Magicbane is an athame.
            - Non-cursed athames engrave Elbereth in one turn
                with 100% success rate without dulling.
        - 'a'pplying a mirror at them
            - Now you know why nymphs carry mirrors.
        - 'a'pplying 
            - leather drum
            - drum of earthquake
            - tooled horn
        - Standing on a scroll of Scare Monster.
        - Casting the spell of Scare Monster.


  You've been bringing a knife to a gunfight for long enough.  Ranged attacks
are a gun.  Multishot ranged attacks are a machine gun.

  Expert daggers with GoP will do more damage than Grayswandir.
   - They also outrange Grayswandir by a factor of Str/2
   - Expert daggers are guaranteed for Rogues.  Grayswandir isn't.
   - Grayswandir only works at melee distance.  That's the best way to
       die in NetHack.  (If the monster is in melee range, so are you.)
   - Rogues throwing Expert daggers with the backstab bonus do insane
       amounts of damage.
   - Daggers can be thrown at melee distance.

  What's the catch?  There are two.  The first is that if you don't improve your
armor you're an eggshell with a hammer.  The second is the Rogue Quest.  (Heh
heh heh.)


